WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.350
The loss depends on the prediction,

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.790
and the prediction
depends on the parameters.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.810
We need both links.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:12.160
Differentiating half squared error with
respect to prediction gives prediction

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.410
minus target.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.910
The factor two from the
square cancels the half.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.170
Increasing a weight changes the prediction
in proportion to its matching input.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.510
Increasing the bias changes
the prediction one for one.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.760
The chain rule multiplies the local loss
slope by the local prediction slope,

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.570
giving a separate derivative
for each parameter.

00:00:36.858 --> 00:00:38.508
For target forty five,

00:00:38.978 --> 00:00:43.388
the residual is negative five
and the inputs are one, two.

00:00:44.138 --> 00:00:49.188
The first weight gradient is negative
five times one, giving negative five.

00:00:49.338 --> 00:00:53.828
The second is negative five times two,
giving negative ten.

00:00:54.658 --> 00:00:57.608
The bias gradient is
negative five times one.

00:00:58.038 --> 00:01:02.958
The second weight is more sensitive in
this calculation because its input is

00:01:02.958 --> 00:01:03.468
larger.

00:01:04.078 --> 00:01:07.108
That does not establish greater
usefulness of the feature.

00:01:07.538 --> 00:01:11.618
It shows how input scale enters the
derivative of this particular forward

00:01:11.618 --> 00:01:12.308
path.

00:01:14.442 --> 00:01:18.232
Choose the demonstration learning
rate zero point zero one.

00:01:18.782 --> 00:01:22.492
Gradient descent subtracts that
rate times each derivative.

00:01:23.142 --> 00:01:28.452
Ten minus zero point zero one times
negative five is ten point zero five.

00:01:29.082 --> 00:01:34.192
Five minus zero point zero one times
negative ten is five point one zero.

00:01:34.962 --> 00:01:38.192
The bias similarly becomes
twenty point zero five.

00:01:38.922 --> 00:01:41.592
Subtracting a negative
produces these increases.

00:01:42.442 --> 00:01:45.812
Their direction fits this
underprediction with positive inputs,

00:01:46.282 --> 00:01:49.032
but the rule to remember
is gradient subtraction.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.232
The rate controls the size of the step.

00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:55.847
The source first forms the residual,

00:01:56.337 --> 00:01:58.567
weight gradients and bias gradient.

00:01:59.017 --> 00:02:03.427
Each new weight subtracts the same
learning rate times its own gradient.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:07.687
The bias follows the same rule
with its separate derivative.

00:02:08.677 --> 00:02:13.127
The update returns new values
rather than modifying the old list.

00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:16.477
That makes before and after inspectable,

00:02:16.477 --> 00:02:20.547
and lets the alternative target
start from the original state.

00:02:21.077 --> 00:02:25.507
Shape and finite-value checks
guard this numerical contract.

00:02:25.777 --> 00:02:30.367
They do not replace the calculation or
establish later forecasting quality.

00:02:32.625 --> 00:02:34.945
Hold the same inputs and target fixed,

00:02:34.945 --> 00:02:38.295
and run the new parameters
through the forward rule.

00:02:38.805 --> 00:02:42.415
The first weighted contribution
rises by zero point zero five.

00:02:43.045 --> 00:02:48.315
The second rises by two times
zero point one, or zero point two.

00:02:48.705 --> 00:02:51.655
Add the bias increase
of zero point zero five.

00:02:52.525 --> 00:02:57.195
The prediction rises by zero point three,
reaching forty point three zero.

00:02:58.105 --> 00:03:01.475
Its remaining residual is
negative four point seven zero,

00:03:02.025 --> 00:03:05.195
and half squared error is
eleven point zero four five.

00:03:06.045 --> 00:03:09.275
This is a same-observation
arithmetic check,

00:03:09.365 --> 00:03:11.895
not an unseen-hour performance result.

00:03:13.983 --> 00:03:18.353
What changes if the starting
prediction already equals the target?

00:03:19.043 --> 00:03:20.713
The residual becomes zero,

00:03:21.023 --> 00:03:24.473
so both weight gradients and
the bias gradient become zero.

00:03:24.923 --> 00:03:28.233
Subtracting their scaled values
leaves the parameters unchanged.

00:03:29.223 --> 00:03:31.493
A zero learning rate also
leaves them unchanged

00:03:31.923 --> 00:03:33.203
even when the residual is nonzero.

00:03:33.203 --> 00:03:38.543
The source checks these boundaries and
compares analytic derivatives with central

00:03:38.543 --> 00:03:40.813
finite differences on another input.

00:03:41.523 --> 00:03:45.363
Our current successful step does not
guarantee that every learning rate or

00:03:45.363 --> 00:03:46.953
later example improves.

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:51.273
The next video changes the target
while keeping the initial state fixed.

